# Defensive: real attendee data must never be committed.
# Attendee lists arrive as Word, CSV, and Excel, so all four are ignored by default.
*.docx
*.doc
*.csv
*.xlsx

# Generated PDFs (badge sheets, test output) stay local.
*.pdf
test/out/
test/output/

# OS / tooling noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# --- Negations: MUST stay last so they win. ---------------------------------
# Re-include ONLY the specific committed fixtures the acceptance tests need.
# Git applies the LAST matching pattern, so these lines must not be moved up.
#
# Deliberately narrow: do NOT broaden this to `!test/fixtures/` or
# `!test/fixtures/**`. A recursive negation would make ANY .csv/.xlsx/.pdf under
# test/fixtures committable, and that directory is precisely where someone would
# drop a real attendee export while testing the importer. Named files only.
# Adding a new fixture in an ignored format means adding a line here for it.
!test/fixtures/import-sample.csv
!test/fixtures/*.json
